course: dictionary
lesson: 9597
title: Stretchy things
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Stretchy means able to stretch: it gets longer or wider when you pull it, and often springs back to its shape afterwards. The context helps you check. «A hamster can stuff its cheeks so full of seeds that its head looks twice as wide, because stretchy pouches run all the way back to its shoulders, like two shopping bags.» The cheeks get so full that the head looks wider, so the pouches must be able to stretch. Swap in "able to stretch" and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Stretchy is also a science word. In materials lessons, pupils pull rubber bands, elastic and balloons to find out which materials are stretchy. Glass and wood are not stretchy, so they do not stretch when pulled. Pupils can fair-test how far each material stretches and compare the results.
explain: «Clothes for sport are often made of stretchy fabric» tells you the fabric moves with your body. Words that mean nearly the same are elastic and flexible. Elastic is the closest match, because it means something that stretches and goes back to shape.
fact: Stretchy means able to stretch, becoming longer or wider when pulled.
fact: Stretchy things often go back to their shape after you let go.
fact: Elastic and flexible are words that mean nearly the same as stretchy.
fact: Some spider silk is stronger than steel for its weight and is very stretchy.
fact: A pelican has a stretchy pouch that works like a net to scoop up fish.
exercise: «A hamster can stuff its cheeks so full of seeds that its head looks twice as wide.» Why can a hamster's cheeks grow so big? | Its cheeks are made of glass | *Its cheek pouches are stretchy and can grow bigger | Its head is made of wood
exercise: Which word means nearly the same as stretchy? | *Elastic | Shiny | Heavy | Cold
exercise: Which material is NOT stretchy? | Rubber band | Elastic | *Glass | Balloon
test: «Clothes for sport are often made of stretchy fabric.» What does stretchy mean? | Wet through | *Able to stretch and often spring back to shape | Hard and cannot bend | Very heavy and cold
test: Pupils want to find out how stretchy a material is. What is a good way to test it? | *Pull it gently and measure how far it stretches | Look at its colour | Throw it in a pond | Read a book about it
exam: «A pelican scoops fish with a stretchy pouch like a net.» What does stretchy mean here? | Hard and sharp | *Able to stretch and grow bigger | Very cold and wet
